## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 · .NET 10 · Integration tests (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell #1: Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** One branch will never execute. If `loaded` is always a regular `User`, the `PremiumUser` assertion is dead code — hidden test gap.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_RegularUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — appears to test polymorphic behavior but only one path ever runs.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell #3: Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Wastes 3 seconds unconditionally. If the notification mechanism becomes slower, this test becomes flaky; if faster, it wastes wall-clock time.

**Integration calibration:** Even for integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` remains a smell — real waits should use polling or async coordination.

**Fix:** Use a polling/retry helper:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk:** Suite slowdown and non-deterministic failures in CI.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Smell #4: Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** Passes as long as no exception is thrown. Doesn't verify record count, data integrity, or uniqueness.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — 100% pass rate even if Insert silently drops rows.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Extended Smell: Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions, none with a message parameter. MSTest failure output shows the first failing assertion but the reason isn't self-describing in CI logs.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned");
```

**Risk:** Minor — slower diagnosis in CI failure logs but not a correctness issue.

---

### ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Written)

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear Arrange/Act/Assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, negative assertion proves deletion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count is self-documenting (3 inserts → `AreEqual(3, ...)`) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate async pattern with a verifying assertion |

The fixture setup is well-scoped — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test (no General Fixture smell). Using in-memory SQLite avoids the Mystery Guest smell while still exercising real SQL.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 focused tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll/retry | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to assertions | ~3 min |

Address #1–#3 first — they all risk false-pass scenarios where broken code looks green.
